<!--
    Moo Launcher's mark: a front-facing cow head, flat white, no stroke, no gradient.

    A familiar silhouette rather than an abstract mark, because the icon has to survive a
    small render - an abstract two-element shape reads as anonymous at that size where a
    recognisable outline does not.

    The ears do the identifying work. Round lobes read as a bear; a cow's ear is a
    horizontal teardrop - broad where it meets the skull, tapering outward and slightly
    down to a rounded tip. They are part of the outer contour rather than shapes laid over
    the head, so the whole silhouette stays one closed path and the eyes and nostrils can
    be real holes under evenOdd. That is also what lets this same path serve as the
    monochrome layer for themed icons.

    108x108 is the adaptive-icon canvas; the path is drawn to the 72x72 safe zone and the
    group below pulls it in further so no mask shape crowds an ear tip.
-->
